{
  "claim": "For non-headline neocloud rate-card series outside the 14-day gate, using analog alone will reduce pinball loss by better representing the timing and size of discrete published-median changes.",
  "mechanism": "Provider repricing or offer turnover can change which offers determine a rate-card median, producing steps separated by periods of persistence. The hypothesis is that analogous aggregate histories across series capture these step-and-persistence patterns better than the current equal-weight blend.",
  "spec": {
    "when": {
      "all": [
        {"fact": "cls", "op": "==", "value": "neocloud_rate_card"},
        {"fact": "gate14", "op": "==", "value": false},
        {"fact": "in37", "op": "==", "value": false}
      ]
    },
    "do": {
      "action": "members_only",
      "members": ["analog"]
    }
  },
  "falsification": "Reject if pooled skill fails to rise overall or in either selection half, fewer than 200 cells across at least five series change, headline pooled skill falls, or fewer than 90% of the 2000 ISO-week block bootstrap resamples show improvement.",
  "prior_ids_used": [],
  "expects": "I expect a modest pooled-skill improvement with headline forecasts unchanged and enough changed cells to meet the breadth requirement. In the reported ungated neocloud rate-card slices, analog beats the current system at all three horizons: +0.209 versus -0.005 at one day, +0.171 versus +0.117 at three days, and +0.175 versus +0.099 at seven days. These aggregates motivate the candidate but do not establish its performance after excluding headline series, its consistency across selection halves, or its bootstrap acceptance."
}
